# Cloudflare Pages headers. Build assets under /_astro/ and /pagefind/ are
# content-hashed (the filename changes whenever the content does), so they are
# safe to cache for a year. Without this, Cloudflare's short default TTL forces
# revalidation round-trips for returning visitors.

# Baseline security hardening, applied to every response. These three are safe
# to enforce site-wide (they don't depend on page content). A Content-Security-
# Policy is intentionally NOT set here yet: the Pyodide runtime is imported from
# the jsDelivr CDN and needs wasm-eval, so a CSP must be authored and verified
# against the live deploy before enforcing - tracked as a follow-up.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/pagefind/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Static brand assets (not hashed) — a week is a safe middle ground.
/og/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
/favicon.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
